[00:17.44] One creature I return to, one habit I neglect
[00:19.53] I cannot slow the pace at which I yearn
[00:24.38] Frank and I unabashed, I become a frozen servant
[00:31.08] Smiling, asking nothing in return
[00:36.00] Fang-tooth, woman foaming at the mouth as she addressed me
[00:42.14] Not with moving lips, but with the rabid wild arresting
[00:47.91] Words not yet intended to identify emotion
[00:49.87] Scrawling bold and oblique in my head
[00:52.26] Ive hung out at your service jobs
[00:55.17] Ive watched you wait and be ignored
[00:59.17] Bled into the clatter, as they sipped at what you poured
[01:03.14] I cling to your perimeter as you float in their margins
[01:05.20] Oblivious to being stung, there satellite becomes my sun
[01:07.14] Ive flown into that trap before, when things have gotten dark
[01:08.70] In the depths of stranger's glances lays the most ferocious spark
[01:10.32] ()
[01:31.73] Most freedom is deceiving, if such a thing exists
[01:33.64] When I was young I knew, but didnt care
[01:35.24] Faces change and shape to represent the same old beast
[01:37.02] I want to flee but I can only stare
[01:38.37] Its the sound a captive heart makes as it sizzles into vapor
[01:39.79] The title hum of fondness like a spike-wave oscillator
[01:41.36] The rabid UV grin that beckons me into approaching
[01:45.09] Grasping as it recedes into space
[01:45.88] Who greets me first when I arive, who breaking into my half-shut eyes?
[01:47.16] Its in the blaze of your embrace where I feel more real and alive
[01:47.98] The bosom of one thousand watts into my skin into my guts
[01:49.04] Running circles in my mind, now, on record, terrified
[01:50.12] That porch we hit the first time, so badly, I died
